{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TQF4NgmZoRMRdrB8AWPRDw","type":"tool_result","content":"12:## 1. The most expensive lesson: a fake +28 % that passed every gate\n33:## 2. Retired by measurement\n52:## 3. The negatives that were really instrumentation failures\n71:## 4. Conditionally retired — re-open after the draft-head fine-tune\n88:## 4b. Killed inside the winning iteration — the radix top-k's two dead levers (ladder 1.2, 2026-08-20)\n119:## 5. What the negatives taught\n=== traps ===\n8:## 1. How a number becomes trustworthy here\n25:## 2. The trap that created rule 2\n32:## 3. The trap that created rule 3\n42:## 4. The traps that created rule 6\n52:## 5. The probe-distribution trap\n64:## 6. Counting the wrong quantity\n75:## 7. Host time is not critical-path time\n80:## 8. Instruments that cannot see themselves\n95:## 9. Self-checks that cry wolf are still worth keeping\n102:## 10. Process traps in the harness itself\n116:## 11. Gate the shape range the engine spans\n125:## 12. The engine stops reproducing itself part-way through a long run, so \"bit-identical token ids\" is not a test there\n179:## 13. A gate that passed, reported as a failure, because the probe it rode on kept no records\n200:## 14. A phase that ran nothing, and reported \"finished\"\n=== kernel-opt ===\n14:## 1. The transformations that generalised\n20:### 1.1 \"Read B once\" — amortise a weight read across every row that uses it\n43:### 1.2 Thread-per-output is wrong at decode shapes\n56:### 1.3 Stage more per barrier\n67:## 2. Structural wins\n69:### 2.1 Full-step CUDA graph (F44)\n78:### 2.2 The arena (F44, F83)\n93:### 2.3 Adaptive verify width (F49, F59, F63)\n102:### 2.4 Fork/join the kv chain (F57)\n107:### 2.5 Don't recompute a prefix that cannot have changed — cache the main-KV (ladder 1.0, 2026-08-20)\n206:### 2.6 A selection sort is not a top-k — single-CTA radix select (ladder 1.2, 2026-08-20)\n304:## 3. Precision and layout\n318:## 4. What every adopted change has in common\n=== ctx-scaling ===\n6:## The claim this page retires\n25:## Two mechanisms made it invisible, and both were structural\n42:## The attribution\n64:## What this changes\n80:## The rule this produces\n93:## Status — 1.0 is done, and the term it removed came off the measured slope\n117:## Status — 1.2 is done too, and it found a term the profile could not see\n144:## What is left of the term","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"16d3a2cb-0895-4089-9bd7-f8432e10d535","uuid":"ea90f283-e7aa-4f3d-9cbd-2aaf06cecd98","timestamp":"2026-08-20T10:48:03.902Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"12:## 1. The most expensive lesson: a fake +28 % that passed every gate\n33:## 2. Retired by measurement\n52:## 3. The negatives that were really instrumentation failures\n71:## 4. Conditionally retired — re-open after the draft-head fine-tune\n88:## 4b. Killed inside the winning iteration — the radix top-k's two dead levers (ladder 1.2, 2026-08-20)\n119:## 5. What the negatives taught\n=== traps ===\n8:## 1. How a number becomes trustworthy here\n25:## 2. The trap that created rule 2\n32:## 3. The trap that created rule 3\n42:## 4. The traps that created rule 6\n52:## 5. The probe-distribution trap\n64:## 6. Counting the wrong quantity\n75:## 7. Host time is not critical-path time\n80:## 8. Instruments that cannot see themselves\n95:## 9. Self-checks that cry wolf are still worth keeping\n102:## 10. Process traps in the harness itself\n116:## 11. Gate the shape range the engine spans\n125:## 12. The engine stops reproducing itself part-way through a long run, so \"bit-identical token ids\" is not a test there\n179:## 13. A gate that passed, reported as a failure, because the probe it rode on kept no records\n200:## 14. A phase that ran nothing, and reported \"finished\"\n=== kernel-opt ===\n14:## 1. The transformations that generalised\n20:### 1.1 \"Read B once\" — amortise a weight read across every row that uses it\n43:### 1.2 Thread-per-output is wrong at decode shapes\n56:### 1.3 Stage more per barrier\n67:## 2. Structural wins\n69:### 2.1 Full-step CUDA graph (F44)\n78:### 2.2 The arena (F44, F83)\n93:### 2.3 Adaptive verify width (F49, F59, F63)\n102:### 2.4 Fork/join the kv chain (F57)\n107:### 2.5 Don't recompute a prefix that cannot have changed — cache the main-KV (ladder 1.0, 2026-08-20)\n206:### 2.6 A selection sort is not a top-k — single-CTA radix select (ladder 1.2, 2026-08-20)\n304:## 3. Precision and layout\n318:## 4. What every adopted change has in common\n=== ctx-scaling ===\n6:## The claim this page retires\n25:## Two mechanisms made it invisible, and both were structural\n42:## The attribution\n64:## What this changes\n80:## The rule this produces\n93:## Status — 1.0 is done, and the term it removed came off the measured slope\n117:## Status — 1.2 is done too, and it found a term the profile could not see\n144:## What is left of the term","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
