{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeELD4a47AHirW7kSdohb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GQ1QtaGd4Jpw6CAZxTihm8","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > evidence/decode_loop/COMMIT_MSG_1p9.txt <<'EOF'\n1.9: the engine's prefill races in the compressed layers above ~192 positions -- localised, bounded, and it was never the decode loop\n\nWHAT WAS MEASURED. build/decode does not reproduce its own PREFILL. Not the decode loop, not\naccumulated drift, not per-process state, and not \"part-way through a long run\": it is\n`compressed_attn_forward`, it fires on any prefill of about 192 positions or more, and it fires\nagain on the identical point four times inside ONE process. Six A/B experiments, no kernel changed.\n\n  1. NOT THE DECODE LOOP. New DSV4_STEPHASH writes one line per verify carrying that step's whole\n     causal chain in dataflow order (mkv -> mx -> din -> draft -> lg -> acc/corr), so two runs diff\n     to the first differing FIELD. On exactly 1.0's divergent arm: point 0 (ctx 5) identical at\n     every field of all 72 verifies; points 1 and 2 diverge at VERIFY 0, with mkv and mx -- the\n     draft's persistent inputs, both pure functions of the prefill -- already different before the\n     first draft ran.  stephash_verdict_AB.txt\n\n  2. FIRST COMPRESSED LAYER. DSV4_HASH=2 (made word-wise and chunked so it can reach real context)\n     hashes all 43 prefill layers. At PSp 5: 43/43 identical. At PSp 3071: layers 0 and 1 -- both\n     ratio 0, pure sliding -- byte-identical, and layer 2, the first ratio-4 layer, first to differ.\n     Every \"first differing layer\" in all six experiments has ratio 4. Not one has ratio 0.\n\n  3. THE THRESHOLD IS 160 -> 192 AND IT IS SHARP. Two length ladders x two runs, 43 layers hashed\n     per point: clean at 16/32/64/128/129/132/136/144/160 -- ten point-comparisons, 430 layer\n     hashes, zero differences -- and 41 of 43 layers differing at 192, 256, 512, 1024, 2048, 2560\n     and 3071. Not the sliding WINDOW (128): 129 through 160 are above it and clean.\n     lhash_L.txt, lhash_W.txt\n\n  4. IT IS A RACE. DSV4_ARENA_ZERO=1 on BOTH arms reproduces the identical verdict, so the arena is\n     dead at the lengths where the defect lives and not only at Finding 61's. Then the decisive\n     one: the same sweep point run four times in ONE process disagrees with itself, first differing\n     layer 2/4/12/28 across the pairs and a different pattern in a second process. Same addresses,\n     same buffer contents, four answers.  lhash_Z.txt, lhash_R.txt\n\n  5. EXONERATED at those lengths: everything the sliding layers do -- k_embed, k_hc_expand,\n     hc_pre/hc_post, rmsnorm, mla_cache_kv, mla_forward, and moe_forward INCLUDING its atomicAdd\n     counting-sort grouping, which this ladder entry had nominated first. The residue is exactly\n     compressor_forward, indexer_forward and sparse_attn. Item 1.10 opens to name which.\n\nWHY THE SERVER LOOKED CLEAN, AND WHY THAT IS NOT A CONTRADICTION. 1.5's 16 legs at ctx 1,656-12,410\nwere byte-identical across two server starts because dsv4-server prefills through\ncblock_verify_step (kernels/compressed_decode.cu) in EXT_CHUNK = 64-row chunks and never issues a\ncompressed prefill call wide enough to reach the threshold, while build/decode prefills through\ncblock_prefill_cache (kernels/compressed_attn.cu) in one call as wide as the prompt. Two binaries,\ntwo prefills, and no bit-exactness result on one transfers to the other. Nothing in this repo said\nthat before. No landed number is retracted.\n\nWHAT IT COSTS THE LADDER. Invariant 1 is now BOUNDED rather than vague: token-id bit-exactness is a\nVALID gate at 160 prefill positions and below -- including the canonical 6-id gate prompt -- and is\nreliably invalid above ~192 on build/decode. Buffer memcmp stays the substitute above it.\n\nTWO WAYS A NUMBER PROVED UNTRUSTWORTHY, both written up:\n  * tests/gate_scratch_init proved compressed_attn_forward poison-independent AT EVERY LENGTH 1..29,\n    and Finding 61 quoted that as the retraction exonerating the prefill chain -- a sentence still\n    carried verbatim in two kernel files. The defect starts between 160 and 192. The gate stops six\n    times short of the regime its verdict was used to close. Both comments now state the range.\n  * DSV4_STEPHASH_LVL=1 writes its two skipped hashes as ZERO, and the comparator read equal as\n    exonerated: it printed \"mkv, main_x and the draft input all MATCH ... the DSpark draft chain is\n    the nondeterministic component\" -- the opposite subsystem, manufactured by the level flag. The\n    tool now excludes all-zero-on-both-sides fields, prints them as NOT MEASURED, and attaches a\n    caveat to any verdict resting on them.\n\nTHE SHIPPED PATH IS UNTOUCHED. Every addition is behind a getenv and off by default. Point 0 of the\ninstrumented binary is BYTE-IDENTICAL, all 266 ids, to the archived genout_1p0_off.txt taken before\nboth 1.5 and 1.9; the first-token GATE and the LOSSLESS GATE PASS in all twelve arms.\n\nNO KERNEL CHANGED, so ladder rule 5 is live: the next iteration takes the highest-expected-value\nkernel item even if it is less certain.\n\nwiki: measurement-and-traps.md §25 (a gate quoted past its range), §26 (a field that was never\ncomputed compares equal), §27 (build/decode and dsv4-server do not share a prefill);\nnegative-results.md §4f (arena and per-process state, both killed); README state table.\nEOF\ngit add -A && git commit -q -F evidence/decode_loop/COMMIT_MSG_1p9.txt && git log --oneline -1","description":"Commit the 1.9 result"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1115,"cache_read_input_tokens":232080,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1115},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"80aa6eab-ae5c-4b4b-8536-b909e02d025d","uuid":"6da438f0-076b-4bd9-9194-6f124a789090","timestamp":"2026-08-20T16:41:02.841Z","request_id":"req_011CeELD39UsJ5vxPJgooM7M"}
