{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeELSYBLtf1j9mDv5MHom","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Iteration 4 complete. Item **1.9** is done and marked; the commit message is staged for the loop driver (`.claude/settings.json` denies `git add/commit/push` to me — `scripts/decode_loop.sh` commits from `evidence/decode_loop/COMMIT_MSG_1p9.txt` and pushes).\n\n## What was measured\n\nAlmost every premise in the ladder entry was wrong. It is **not** the decode loop, not drift, not per-process state, and not \"part-way through a long run.\"\n\n**`build/decode`'s PREFILL races inside the compressed (`ratio != 0`) layers, from ~192 prefill positions up.** Six A/B experiments, twelve runs:\n\n| step | finding | evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| new `DSV4_STEPHASH` (per-verify causal chain) on 1.0's exact divergent arm | point 0 identical at every field of 72 verifies; points 1 & 2 diverge at **verify 0**, `mkv`/`mx` already different before the first draft | `stephash_verdict_AB.txt` |\n| `DSV4_HASH=2` per-layer prefill hash, run-to-run | PSp 5: 43/43 identical. PSp 3071: layers 0–1 (`ratio 0`) identical, layer **2** (first `ratio 4`) first to differ | `lhash_H.txt` |\n| length ladder 16→3071 | clean at 16/32/64/128; 41 of 43 layers differ at 256 and every length above | `lhash_L.txt` |\n| refined ladder 128→256 | clean at 129/132/136/144/**160**; racing at **192**. 430 layer hashes below the threshold, zero differences. Not `WINDOW`=128 | `lhash_W.txt` |\n| `DSV4_ARENA_ZERO=1` on **both** arms | identical verdict — arena dead at the lengths that matter, not just Finding 61's | `lhash_Z.txt` |\n| same point ×4 **inside one process** | four different prefills, first differing layer 2/4/12/28 → **a race, not state** | `lhash_R_within.txt` |\n\nEverything the sliding layers do is exonerated at every length to 3071 — including the MoE's `atomicAdd` counting-sort grouping, which the entry had nominated first. Residue: `compressor_forward`, `indexer_forward`, `sparse_attn`. Item **1.10** opens to name which, with the probe and two zero-code first steps (`DSV4_TOPK_RADIX=0`, `NO_IXGEMM=1`) specified.\n\n**The server is not a contradiction:** `dsv4-server` prefills through `cblock_verify_step` in `EXT_CHUNK`=64-row chunks; `build/decode` through `cblock_prefill_cache` in one prompt-wide call. Different code, and no bit-exactness result on one transfers to the other. No landed number is retracted.\n\n**No kernel changed**, so ladder rule 5 is now live and I wrote that at the top of the entry — the next iteration must take a kernel item.\n\nTwo traps written up: `gate_scratch_init` proved poison-independence *at lengths 1..29* and that was quoted as unbounded exoneration (defect starts at 160→192; both kernel comments now state the range), and my own `DSV4_STEPHASH_LVL=1` wrote unmeasured hashes as zero, so the comparator read equal-as-exonerated and named the opposite subsystem — fixed in the tool.\n\nShipped path verified untouched: point 0's full 266 ids are byte-identical to `genout_1p0_off.txt` archived before both 1.5 and 1.9; GATE and LOSSLESS GATE PASS in all twelve arms. `stephash_run.sh` is in `detach_audit.sh`'s pattern list, and the audit reports all detached."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":402,"cache_read_input_tokens":246566,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":402},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"80aa6eab-ae5c-4b4b-8536-b909e02d025d","uuid":"718abcc4-8f13-4649-b295-73ba6550e0a1","timestamp":"2026-08-20T16:43:59.497Z","request_id":"req_011CeELSVvfFERBCruxuRXi5"}
